<DocsLayout title="LangChain guide | dotfetch" description="Integrate dotfetch with LangChain: native StructuredTools with readable errors, approval and run context, plus per-turn selection for create_agent.">
  <p class="eyebrow">Framework guide</p>
  <h1>LangChain</h1>
  <p class="lead">dotfetch hands LangChain native <code>StructuredTool</code>s. Every call goes through <code>fetcher.execute</code>, failures reach the model as error <code>ToolMessage</code>s, and inside a <code>create_agent</code> agent a middleware picks each model turn's tools.</p>
  <p><a class="pill" href="/Agent-Gantry/docs/frameworks/langchain/advanced/">Advanced LangChain usage →</a></p>

  <h2>Install</h2>
  <CodeBlock lang="bash" code={`uv add "dotfetch[langchain]"   # langchain, langchain-core >= 1.0`} />

  <h2>Basic page: a selected slice of tools</h2>
  <CodeBlock lang="python" code={`from langchain.chat_models import init_chat_model
from dotfetch import DotFetch
from dotfetch.langchain import LangChainAdapter

fetcher = DotFetch()

@fetcher.register(examples=["where is my order", "has order 4471 shipped"])
def get_order_status(order_id: str) -> str:
    """Return the current shipping status for an order."""
    return "in_transit"

await fetcher.sync()
adapter = LangChainAdapter(fetcher)
tools = await adapter.select("has order 4471 shipped?", limit=3)
llm = init_chat_model("openai:gpt-5.5").bind_tools(tools)`} />

  <h2>An agent whose tools change every turn</h2>
  <p>LangChain's <code>create_agent</code> accepts middleware. dotfetch's middleware brings the catalogue with it and narrows the tools offered on each model turn to the ones relevant to the newest message or tool result.</p>
  <CodeBlock lang="python" code={`from langchain.agents import create_agent

agent = create_agent("openai:gpt-5.5", middleware=[await adapter.middleware(limit=5)])
result = await agent.ainvoke({"messages": [("user", "Has order 4471 shipped?")]})`} />

  <h2>What the model sees when a tool fails</h2>
  <p>A failed call raises LangChain's <code>ToolException</code> and the tool sets <code>handle_tool_error=True</code>, so the model receives an error <code>ToolMessage</code> with <code>&lt;type&gt;: &lt;message&gt;</code>, capped at 2,000 characters.</p>
  <div class="callout"><strong>Redact or opt out:</strong> <code>LangChainAdapter(fetcher, error_formatter=redact)</code> rewrites the text the model sees; <code>error_mode="raise"</code> lets <code>ToolExecutionError</code> propagate instead.</div>
</DocsLayout>
